  "conclusion": "A single CNN with one binary output can learn a nondegenerate impurity-reducing split without performing multiclass classification. Gini learned an almost pure digit-1-vs-rest split; entropy learned a balanced multi-digit grouping. A two-convolution version retained the qualitative questions with 79.31% fewer parameters, but its entropy reduction fell materially, so the three-convolution network remains the stronger splitter."
